From 5c57db75f99180811a1afe3964015f3c05206de7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:46:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] coop MoE decode: mixed-K instances, one launch per stage
 for a mixed-K layer

exl3_moe_coop_mk takes per-expert gate/up/down widths (int32 tables, each in
[k_lo, k_hi]) and runs the whole layer in one rot/A/B launch set instead of one
per (Kg, Ku, Kd) group. Kernels are templated on a width range [KLO, KHI]: the
uniform instances are KLO == KHI (same code as before); mixed instances
[1,2], [2,3], [3,4] read each item's width from the tables and dispatch the
K-templated tile body per block (k_dispatch). Mixed instances are held to two
blocks per SM (64 registers) and take the runs in descending expert order, so
with experts numbered in ascending K the heavy items start first.

The gate/up tail split now picks its factor from a wave-time model (a
part-filled wave takes max(fill, 0.69) of a full one, a split 5% extra) instead
of filling one wave exactly; it still only applies below three waves.

GB10, MiniMax 2.15 pack TP2-rank layer types, live decode routing, L2 flushed,
per-layer coop time, per-K-group launches (5e1e37de) -> one mixed-K launch:
  112x(2,2,2)+16x(2,2,3) (45 layers): c=1 466 -> 436 us, c=4 978 -> 941 us
  88x(2,2,2)+30x(2,2,3)+10x(3,3,3) (12 layers): c=1 529 -> 486 us, c=4 1112 -> 999 us
A mixed instance on a uniform-K layer is bit-identical to the uniform launch;
against the split launches the mixed-K layer differs only in the order slots
are summed (rel 1e-4..6e-4). fp32-reference error 6.4e-4..6.6e-4 (split same,
mixedk 6.4e-4..6.7e-4); robustness and counter-reuse checks vs mixedk <= 8.9e-4.
